  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _stepData:
  - _stepName: movement
    _description: 'Welcome to the Gridlock Gladiators tutorial.

      Let''s start
      with movement.

      You can freely move on the side that matches your character
      color.

      Move to the highlighted panels.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: normal
    _description: 'Now let''s try attacking.

      Attacking your opponent builds
      their damage meter at the top. The higher the opponents damage meter is, the
      easier it is to send them flying.

      Try using a normal attack by pressing
      the attack button.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 149171661}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetImageActive
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Weak
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
        - m_Target: {fileID: 714839856}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: set_enabled
          m_Mode: 6
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 1
          m_CallState: 2
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
        - m_Target: {fileID: 714839856}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: set_enabled
          m_Mode: 6
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: combos
    _description: 'Great attack!

      Each gladiator has 4 of these normal attacks.
      You can perform different normal attacks by holding a move direction while
      attacking.

      Try using different normal attacks to get a 7 hit combo.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 149171661}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetImageActive
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Weak
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: strong
    _description: 'Practicing to discover longer combos will allow you to rack up
      damage on your enemies quickly and keep you at an advantage.

      Each normal
      attack has a stronger variation that can be used to send your opponent flying
      into their barrier.

      If the opponent is hit into their barrier enough,
      it will shatter and give you the chance to ring them out.

      Try using
      a strong attack to knockout the test dummy.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 149171661}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetImageActive
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Strong
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
        - m_Target: {fileID: 1359032533}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: ToggleInvincibleBarriers
          m_Mode: 1
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
        - m_Target: {fileID: 428590915}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: set_enabled
          m_Mode: 6
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
        - m_Target: {fileID: 1359032533}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: ToggleInvincibleBarriers
          m_Mode: 1
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: specials
    _description: "Nice knockout!\nIn addition to your normal moves, you also have
      special moves that can be used in battle.\nYour special moves are contained
      in a deck and randomized at the start of each match. \nOnly two special moves
      can be used at any time. You can tell which ones are available by looking at
      the icons over your character's head. \nIn order to perform a special move,
      you need to have enough energy stored.\nYou can tell how much energy you have
      stored by looking at the energy meter in the bottom of the screen. The meter
      will charge automatically, but it will charge faster if you attack your opponent.\nThe
      amount of energy required to perform a special move can be determined from
      the icon color, shape, and the number attached to it.\nTry using all 8 special
      moves."
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 52024570}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetActive
          m_Mode: 6
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: reload
    _description: 'Once you run out of abilities you''ll have to wait a short while
      for your deck to reload.

      You can manually reload your deck anytime you''d
      like if you want a different pair of abilities to use. You''ll be completely
      immobile while initiating the reload so use this carefully.

      Try reloading
      your deck.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 149171661}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetImageActive
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Shuffle
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    _onStepComplete:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 999576671}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: 
          m_MethodName: SetTrigger
          m_Mode: 5
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: Maximize
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - _stepName: burst
    _description: 'Next we''ll cover defense.

      If you ever find yourself in
      trouble you can use a burst counter.

      A burst counter is a defensive
      ability that can stop your momentum, destroy projectiles in range, and knock
      your opponent away from you. It''s really useful for breaking out of combos
      and putting you back in the fight.

      Try using a burst counter to prevent
      yourself from hitting the ring barrier after being hit.'
    _onStepBegin:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 149171661}
